Module overexall "Over Exall" {
  Description "Exall: three hundred people on a ridge in the Brack, and a drift-whale hung by its lip from the steeple, sinking a house-height every dusk.".

  // The whale lies along the ridge: its chin on the steeple of St Ebba's, its belly over the Cross, its tail past the Edge.
  Place brack "the Brack" is region within imbar.
  Place edge "the Edge" is wilderness within brack at 0, 0.
  Place exall "Exall" is settlement within brack at 0, 1.
  Place lodger_site "the Lodger" is site within brack at 1, 1.

  Place tarpaulin "the Tarpaulin" is building within exall.
  Place bakehouse "Elley's bakehouse" is building within exall.
  Place cottage "Dorcas Holle's cottage" is building within exall.
  Place kirk "St Ebba's" is site within exall.
  Place steeple "the steeple" is level within kirk.

  Place road "the Edge road" is room within edge at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place field "the Windlass Field" is room within edge at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place cross "the Cross" is room within exall at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place row "the Pits" is room within exall at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place stack "the peat-stack" is room within exall at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place taproom "the Tarpaulin's taproom" is room within tarpaulin at 0, 0.
  Place loft "the pigeon loft" is room within tarpaulin at 0, 1.
  Place oven "the bakehouse" is room within bakehouse at 0, 0.
  Place bedroom "Dorcas Holle's room" is room within cottage at 0, 0.
  Place foot "the foot of the steeple" is room within kirk at 0, 0.
  Place bell_chamber "the bell-chamber" is room within steeple at 0, 0.
  Place ledge "the jaw-ledge" is room within steeple at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Place back "the Lodger's back" is room within lodger_site at 0, 0 outdoors.
  Place shoulder "the Lodger's shoulder" is room within lodger_site at 1, 0 outdoors.

  Passage way_in "the last of the Edge road" is road between road and cross taking 20 minutes.
  Passage field_path "the track along the Edge" is path between road and field taking 10 minutes.
  Passage tarp_door "the Tarpaulin's door" is door between cross and taproom.
  Passage bake_door "the bakehouse door" is door between cross and oven.
  Passage cottage_door "Dorcas Holle's door" is door between cross and bedroom.
  Passage row_way "the way down to the Pits" is path between cross and row taking 5 minutes.
  Passage stack_way "the lane to the peat-stack" is path between cross and stack taking 5 minutes.
  Passage lych "the lych-gate" is gate between cross and foot.
  Passage steeple_stair "the steeple door" is stair between foot and bell_chamber.
  Passage bell_ladder "the ladder to the ledge" is ladder between bell_chamber and ledge.
  Passage lip_ladder "the rope ladder up the Lodger's lip" is ladder between ledge and back taking 10 minutes.
  Passage back_path "along the spine" is path between back and shoulder taking 10 minutes.
  Passage loft_ladder "the loft ladder" is ladder between taproom and loft.
  Passage roofs "the gutter over the roofs" is ladder between loft and ledge hidden until roofs_known needing climbing or rope taking 20 minutes.
  Passage kite_ride "Saley's kite" is path between field and back hidden until kite_known taking 30 minutes.

  // ── The road and the Edge ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe road_scene at road when true "The sun is out, and it is raining on the town. A sign is nailed to a post at the top of the road, over an older sign: EXALL. PLEASE DO NOT FEED THE WHALE. Under it, in a different hand: WE HAVE TRIED.".
  Observe road_drip at road as ambience when true "The rain falls in a column the width of the ridge, out of a sky with nothing in it, and stops exactly at the last stile.".
  Observe field_scene at field when true "A wind-raked moor at the edge of the ridge, with a view of three valleys. A drum of cable stands staked into the turf, and the cable goes up at a long slant to a kite the size of a barn door.".

  // ── The Cross ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe cross_scene at cross when true "The market stands in a shadow the shape of a barn door turned over. The belly of the Lodger is slate-grey and wet, and goes on out of sight in both directions. Stallholders have rigged tarred sails for umbrellas.".
  Observe cross_hum at cross as ambience when true "Every pewter pot in the square hums one low note, a little after the whale breathes out.".
  Observe cross_low_1 at cross when low() == 1 "The weathercock is gone into the whale's lip. The belly has settled a house-height since morning, and the chimney-smoke goes up and flattens against it.".
  Observe cross_low_2 at cross when low() == 2 "The Lodger hangs at the height of the eaves. Washing lines run from the High Street's gutters up into the wet grey, where it has begun to carry them.".
  Observe cross_low_3 at cross when low() == 3 "The belly rests on the highest roofs. Tiles tick and shift. Nobody is in the High Street who does not have to be.".
  Observe cross_rising at cross when risingTold(party) "The belly stands off the roofs now, a hundred feet up, and tight as a drum. The rain has stopped, and there is clear sky at the edges.".

  // ── The Tarpaulin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe taproom_scene at taproom when true "A long room under a sail of tarred canvas where the ceiling began to weep. The settles stand in bowls. Cream is not served.".
  Observe loft_scene at loft when true "Pigeons, a hundred of them, all facing the same way. Through the slats you can see the underside of the whale a hand's breadth off, shining.".

  // ── the Pits ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe row_scene at row when true "A lane of pits and drying racks at the bottom of the hill, downwind of everything and always has been. Fifty hides hang here in rows. The air is thick enough to lean on.".
  Observe row_dark_marks at row when day(clock) >= 2 "Four bare hooks on the end rack. Along the cobbles beneath them runs a long, wet, tapering groove, as if a rope had been trailed.".

  // ── The peat-stack ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe stack_scene at stack when true "Forty cords of cut peat stand under a long roof of slates, stacked to the ridge, brown and square and sweet. It is the whole warmth of Exall until April.".

  // ── The bakehouse and the cottage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe oven_scene at oven when true "Three ovens in a brick wall, and a trough. On the shelf over the trough sits a crock with a muslin cap, and nobody puts anything on the shelf beside it.".
  Observe bedroom_scene at bedroom when true "A bed with a patchwork quilt, a chair, and a window that looks at nothing but the Lodger. The glass hums. On the sill stands a handkerchief, folded, ironed, and clearly not for use.".

  // ── St Ebba's ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe foot_scene at foot when true "The tower of St Ebba's goes up through the roofs of Exall and into the whale. A bell-rope as thick as a wrist hangs in the porch, bound with cloth at the top where it goes into the dark.".
  Observe bell_scene at bell_chamber when true "One great bell, its clapper wrapped in felt and fleece. The floor is wet. The louvres on the north side have been shouldered open from outside, and filled, softly, with grey.".
  Observe ledge_scene at ledge when true "A stone gallery round the spire, open to the wind. The Lodger's lip is hooked over the spire's shoulder like a man's chin on a gatepost: an eye the size of a cartwheel, shut, with a lashless lid, and under it a flank that rises and falls.".
  Observe ledge_breath at ledge as ambience when true "Each breath out smells of rain, and stone, and a little of the sea.".

  // ── The Edge road's far side ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe back_scene at back when true "You are standing on the animal. The skin runs away under your feet in a long grey slope, warm as a flank, and the slope rises and falls. Along the spine the wind is warm.".
  Observe shoulder_scene at shoulder when true "The shoulder is where the lip ends and the great muscle begins. The skin is thick here and scarred in long seams. It moves up and down, slowly, under a wind that comes from very far away.".

  // ── What can be known ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lodger_known "A drift-whale has come down on Exall in the night and hung itself by the lip on St Ebba's steeple. It sinks about a house-height each dusk and will be on the roofs on the fourth morning.".
  Discovery lane_lost "The drift-whales keep to lanes in the high cloud. The Shales folk of Wickering have driven a rain-cloud through the lanes for nine generations, and this autumn it went into a glasshouse and put them out.".
  Discovery candlemas_known "Dorcas Holle calls the Lodger Candlemas. It came down on Exall sixty-one years ago, and rose again, and took her up with it.".
  Discovery fire_known "Sixty-one years ago Exall lit every hearth at once on the third night, and the smoke raised the whale.".
  Discovery leaven_known "The Old Leaven that makes Exall's Skyloaf came out of the whale: a lump of grey sourness that fell on a windowsill the morning it rose.".
  Discovery rank_known "The Lodger takes only what is rank: sour hides, old dough, tan-liquor. It is starving, and it is looking for the smell of what it is.".
  Discovery answer_heard "The Lodger answers the bell. At noon a third below, a long way off, something hums along.".
  Discovery iron_known "An old harpoon head is lodged in the Lodger's shoulder, grown over with skin. It is stamped with a small cloud and S.O. CLOUDGATE.".
  Discovery strike_known "Captain Ottoline Saley of Cloudgate will fire on the Lodger at dusk on the third day if it is still hanging.".
  Discovery roofs_known "Sab Thord goes out over the roofs from the pigeon loft to the ledge.".
  Discovery kite_known "Captain Saley's kite can carry a company from the Windlass Field to the Lodger's back.".
  Discovery barbel_known "At night the Lodger lowers a feeler a hundred feet long into the Pits and takes the rankest hide off the rack.".
  Discovery peat_known "The town's peat-stack holds forty cords, and every hearth lit at once would use most of it.".
}
